<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Požega, Croatia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Požega is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a> region of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, in a fertile valley ringed by hills. A county seat of the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, it was taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1537 and returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule in 1688, after which it again became the seat of Požega County. It is the centre of a well-known wine-growing district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pozega-croatia.jpg" alt="Požega, Croatia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andres rus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holy_Ghost_-_Pozega.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
